          %p
            For relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            see
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory+and+physics"} higher category theory and physics
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics"} geometry of physics
          %h2#Lurie References
          %p
            Both approaches to higher geometry are described, in the special case of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+algebraic+geometry"} derived algebraic geometry
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Derived+Algebraic+Geometry"} Derived Algebraic Geometry
          %p
            The gros topos approach is described, in the case of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopical+algebraic+geometry"} homotopical algebraic geometry
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bertrand+To%C3%ABn"}> Bertrand Toën
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gabriele+Vezzosi"} Gabriele Vezzosi
              = succeed "," do
                %em Homotopical algebraic geometry II: geometric stacks and applications
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0404373"} arXiv:math/0404373
          %p A general exposition of the petit topos approach is proposed in
          %ul
            %li#Lurie
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Structured+Spaces"} Structured Spaces
              \.
          %p In
          %ul
            %li#Lawvere
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bill+Lawvere"}> Bill Lawvere
              ,
              %em Axiomatic cohesion
              Theory and Applications of Categories, Vol. 19, No. 3, 2007, pp. 41–49. (
              %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/19/3/19-03.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            an axiomatization of generalized geometry is proposed in terms of 1-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"}> category theory
            \. The evident generalization of this to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+theory"} (∞,1)-category theory
            provides an axiomatization for higher geometry. This is discussed at
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"}> cohesive (∞,1)-topos
              \.
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
                ,
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Higher+Topos+Theory+in+Physics"} Higher Topos Theory in Physics
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.11026"}> arXiv:2311.11026
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Luigi+Alfonsi"}> Luigi Alfonsi
                , §1 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Higher geometry in physics
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Encyclopedia+of+Mathematical+Physics+2nd+ed"} Encyclopedia of Mathematical Physics 2nd ed
                %strong 4
                Elsevier (2024) 39-61 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.07308"}> arXiv:2312.07308
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/B978-0-323-95703-8.00209-3"} doi:10.1016/B978-0-323-95703-8.00209-3
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://shop.elsevier.com/books/encyclopedia-of-mathematical-physics/szabo/978-0-323-95703-8"} ISBN:978-0-323-95703-8
